# What `mui init` writes as `build-aui.hxml`.
#
# It lives here rather than in `mui` because what a build for this backend needs
# -- which libraries, which generator macro, which output -- is ours to state,
# and `mui` had no way of keeping six of these honest. `$MAIN` is the only thing
# substituted.
-cp src
-lib mui
-lib aui
-D mui_backend=aui
-D jvm
--jvm build/app-logic.jar
--macro aui.macros.ComposeGenerator.register()
--macro mui.macros.Bind.all()
--macro aui.kui.Platform.registerWithKui()
# The backend's vocabulary, so `ui()` can check a tag against what this backend
# actually declares. Without it a markup screen does not compile at all, naming
# neither the missing line nor the build file -- a poor welcome for the way a UI
# is meant to be written here.
#
# Building this backend's own controls is the default; `-D mui_nodes` is the way
# back, for a tree that is going to be sent rather than drawn.
--macro aui.nui.Vocabulary.registerWithMui()
--main $MAIN
